{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/978786-ideas-for-punishments-for-those-who-commit-crimes-against-the-moon","id":978786,"title":"Ideas for punishments for those who commit crimes against the moon.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-29T19:25:55-07:00","id":978786,"title":"Ideas for punishments for those who commit crimes against the moon.","content":"Hello people. <br /> How would a Lune come to punish the forsaken for its crimes? There is a Sheet for a lune in the game? <br /> a werewolf committing a heinous crime like eating human flesh without anyone knowing How the lunes can find out? and what they could do about it?<br /> <br /> There are very few examples in the book of how crime punishment can manifest. I hope that this topic brings different ideas of different players, helping a little more on creating penalties for players with a tendency to commit sins ingame. Turning the punishment it into a cool way to be displayed without breaking the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T20:00:48-07:00","id":978801,"title":"","content":"Keeping in mind that not all lunes are going to care or do something about it.<br /> <br /> In the case of The Herd Must Not Know, a lune with Influence over Wisdom might casually warp the memories of everyone the werewolf is in contact with, or just whoever they come across in the werewolf's territory. They might even warp the mind of the werewolf. I suppose they could stalk them, trying to ensure they are noticed in everything they do until they learn to be hidden. A werewolf who doesn't Cleave to the Human might find others influenced into their relationship, or those they couple with killed or otherwise influenced by the magic of the lunes. It could doom their chances at fertility, or bless them in certain awful scenarios, or take out their displeasure in other ways, trying to drain loci in the territory, or break fetishes open to free spirits and make the werewolf's existence a barren one.<br /> <br /> It's risky, of course, because the more a lune is going to act against a werewolf the more likely it is going to find the werewolf acting against it. It would probably be easiest for the lune to simply try to manipulate another pack to 'teach the oathbreaker a lesson.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-29-2016, 11:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T20:38:06-07:00","id":978824,"title":"","content":"Probably is the easiest way but in terms of ingame narrative it will sound very unlikely to happen. Imagine if you as a player are certain that you comited a crime by mistake and nobody saw it. (You think you are safe) but suddenly some random pack shows up as paladins of justice because a lune just told them about your sin. <br /> Its not a bad way to use the punishment because it brings the possibility to create a entirely new campaign about redemption but its something that just got out of nothing and the player can be &quot;Mad&quot; with the idea that you just summoned a whole pack to punish him by something so secret.<br /> <br /> My campaign is in the middle of a very serious situation where the stakes are ultra high and my player just forgot that eating humans is a bad thing.... Now I cant just bring an entire new plot to punish him and I cant have a &quot;pause&quot; button to slow down the situation and summon a lune to punish him.<br /> I figured he could have sudden dreams of his mouth sewn unable to eat and speak.<br /> When the player wakes up nothing will change in appearances but he will not be able to have the strength to make bites and will vomit when eating any kind of food.<br /> <br /> But my idea do not seem very hardcore as the book says it should be. The book quotes even mention loss of limbs when committing the crime of cannibalism. so.. i do know...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T20:45:33-07:00","id":978829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>magisanctum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/978786-ideas-for-punishments-for-those-who-commit-crimes-against-the-moon?p=978824#post978824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably is the easiest way but in terms of ingame narrative it will sound very unlikely to happen. Imagine if you as a player are certain that you comited a crime by mistake and nobody saw it. (You think you are safe) but suddenly some random pack shows up as paladins of justice because a lune just told them about your sin.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of the reasons the Pure burn off their brands.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My campaign is in the middle of a very serious situation where the stakes are ultra high and my player just forgot that eating humans is a bad thing.... Now I cant just bring an entire new plot to punish him and I cant have a &quot;pause&quot; button to slow down the situation and summon a lune to punish him.<br /> I figured he could have sudden dreams of his mouth sewn unable to eat and speak.<br /> When the player wakes up nothing will change in appearances but he will not be able to have the strength to make bites and will vomit when eating any kind of food.<br /> <br /> But my idea do not seem very hardcore as the book says it should be. The book quotes even mention loss of limbs when committing the crime of cannibalism. so.. i do know... </div> </div> </div>I usually foster corruption, to be honest.<br /> <br /> If you wanted them to be punished, though, all that's required is a particularly zealous werewolf or lune who believes that that PCs breaking of the oath is a matter of more importance than whatever's going on. Considering the mindsets of spirits and werewolves it shouldn't be that hard to find. If you have a particularly honorable werewolf in the pack, they might find a lune whispering to them at night, telling them that something must be done. It doesn't have to pause the combat, but the lune doesn't necessarily care about the pack, or even werewolves. So the fact that they're in a high stakes situation might not matter to them.<br /> <br /> Or they, or another lune, might 'care' deeply about the situation, as much as a spirit such as a lune can. Maybe it has some order from on high to wait, see if the werewolf atones after the fact, and if not, to punish them then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-29-2016, 11:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T07:20:34-07:00","id":979001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>magisanctum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/978786-ideas-for-punishments-for-those-who-commit-crimes-against-the-moon#post978786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello people.<br /> How would a Lune come to punish the forsaken for its crimes? There is a Sheet for a lune in the game?<br /> a werewolf committing a heinous crime like eating human flesh without anyone knowing How the lunes can find out? and what they could do about it?<br /> <br /> There are very few examples in the book of how crime punishment can manifest. I hope that this topic brings different ideas of different players, helping a little more on creating penalties for players with a tendency to commit sins ingame. Turning the punishment it into a cool way to be displayed without breaking the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunes themselves don't need to do anything, any Purity or Honor prone Uratha would take matters into their own hands. For cannibalism? I'd sever their hands and have them eat it. They will regrow it, but it's a painful process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T09:24:58-07:00","id":979099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/978786-ideas-for-punishments-for-those-who-commit-crimes-against-the-moon?p=979001#post979001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For cannibalism? I'd sever their hands and have them eat it. They will regrow it, but it's a painful process.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was trying to avoid something like that in my suggestions. On one hand, it's suitably savage, but on the other, it's basically encouraging an addiction. Like being forced to smoke a pack of cigarettes if you're caught smoking a cigarette, neglecting to realize that there is an addictiveness the punished might find harder to control once finished. I could see some malevolent wolves pretending to be these 'paladins,' doing these types of things in order to foster bans that required increasingly oathbreaking activity.<br /> <br /> That said, as an avid user of Bone Gnaw, I'm curious as to whether or not you could use it to gain a bonus to your highest Skill or Renown, based on your highest Skill or Renown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-30-2016, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T10:17:27-07:00","id":979136,"title":"","content":"I have a character who I am playing that, upon breaking the &quot;don't eat the flesh of man or wolf&quot; tenet in order to kill a pure alpha that out-matched him and was using silver already (he doesn't follow the people do not kill the people tenet, being a garmir who doesn't see the pure as proper uratha.) But in penance for the flesh eating he is going to remove his own eye with a silver knife and let the wound heal naturally with no magical interference, essential body-part removal using silver as a punishment for severe breakage of the oath. Limbs, eyes, the nose, something that would obviously cripple the uratha on a hunt but not render them totally useless. Though eye-removal is not as crippling to an uratha as it could be given wolf-senses compensates for any penalties derived the loss of the eye, in character I think it makes sense still, plus it leaves a rather obvious scar that is going to be a source of shame, not pride.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T11:13:57-07:00","id":979162,"title":"","content":"First determine if spirit witnesses would either be watching in or from the <i>hisil</i>, then figure out if that infomration would make it through the grapevine to Luna's Court.<br /> <br /> If so consider this: Lunes are messengers of Luna, and if Luna, or Powerful Lunes in her Choir/Court became aware of something truly awful done by Forsaken the worst thing the Lunes could do is spread the tale/shameful deed-name and then reward with Renown those forsaken that punish the transgressor appropriately.<br /> <br /> I'd expect the <i>hisil </i>to be filled with snitches who'd love to get the Forsaken in trouble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 09-30-2016, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T10:22:45-07:00","id":980318,"title":"","content":"That sounds like a good basis for a villainous pack. They follow a lune as their totem and are basically a bunch of fanatical douchebags who travel from domain to domain to give horrible punishments to those who break the oath of the Moon. They would rely on spirits ratting other forsaken out, and maybe a gift that lets them read the markings on other werewolves and detect potential oath breakers that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T11:19:42-07:00","id":980349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/978786-ideas-for-punishments-for-those-who-commit-crimes-against-the-moon?p=980318#post980318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds like a good basis for a villainous pack. They follow a lune as their totem and are basically a bunch of fanatical douchebags who travel from domain to domain to give horrible punishments to those who break the oath of the Moon. They would rely on spirits ratting other forsaken out, and maybe a gift that lets them read the markings on other werewolves and detect potential oath breakers that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lune totems drive packs insane, so they wouldn't hold much respect with the community at large. I'd conceal the fact that the spirit is a lune, maybe even from the pack itself. Irralunim rarely shy at breaking taboos, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T12:34:09-07:00","id":980381,"title":"","content":"That's the point. It'd start as a &quot;it seemed like a good idea at the time&quot;.<br /> <br /> They would probably have formed in an area where, due to a recent case of idigam or overly violent war with the pure, most packs were wiped out and most elders killed. Young werewolves pop up (the crisis probably caused lots of lunacy), not really knowing what to do. They gather pieces of information about the oath of the Moon and stuff, the survivors try to organize them into packs and tell them about the tribes. A particularly promising pack forms, and they want to take all that oath of the Moon very seriously, so they go find a lune because what better spirit to enforce the oath, right ? Some survivors seemed to think that was a bad idea, but it's probably just because they're afraid.<br /> <br /> So they start doing their business, tracking whoever broke the oath. They start by being mediators, advising other packs on what to do and helping them out. They build themselves a local reputation. The survivors from the older packs start seriously worrying and making plans to stop all this before it goes wrong, but the lune expected that. The lune had the luck to stumble upon a pack of young naive uratha who looked up to it and now, and it's not about to let a few old wolves ruin everything (it's kind of a weird cult leader at this point). So it starts accusing them of being oath breakers and soon enough, everybody turns against them and the young pack, filled with sadness, does the only thing they can and put them down (before conducting and painful and elaborate atonement ritual).<br /> <br /> It was a sad affair, but they did it, they cleansed their city/county/whatever of oath breakers, but the lune is't satisfied and the pack members themselves know there is more work to be done. There's an entire world to guide on the right path and beware anyone who gets in their way for they carry the will of Mother Moon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T23:46:49-07:00","id":980609,"title":"","content":"I hate and love you right now all - you just make D&amp;D Paladins evil for following good intentions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}